ZEE MUSIC — Power BI model setup and DAX solutions

MODEL SETUP
Create one-to-many, single-direction relationships:
Artist[ArtistKey] 1 -> * Music_Streams[ArtistKey]
Album[AlbumKey] 1 -> * Music_Streams[AlbumKey]
Date[DateKey] 1 -> * Music_Streams[DateKey]
Mark Date as the date table using Date[Date]. Make Date[Date] a Date type and key columns matching whole-number types. Create each measure below separately via Modeling > New measure. Run each EVALUATE query in DAX Query View.

BASE MEASURES (create separately)

[Total Streams] = SUM('Music_Streams'[StreamCount])
[Total Revenue] = SUM('Music_Streams'[RevenueUSD])
[Streaming Records] = COUNTROWS('Music_Streams')
[Average Revenue per Record] = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], [Streaming Records])
[Average Listening Minutes] = AVERAGE('Music_Streams'[MinutesListened])
[Total Skips] = SUM('Music_Streams'[SkipCount])
[Unique Listeners] = DISTINCTCOUNT('Music_Streams'[ListenerID])
[Revenue per Stream] = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], [Total Streams])
[Completed Records] = CALCULATE([Streaming Records], 'Music_Streams'[IsCompleted] = "Yes")
[Not Completed Records] = CALCULATE([Streaming Records], 'Music_Streams'[IsCompleted] = "No")
[Revenue Previous Year] = CALCULATE([Total Revenue], DATEADD('Date'[Date], -1, YEAR))
[Revenue YoY Change] = [Total Revenue] - [Revenue Previous Year]
[Revenue YoY Growth %] = DIVIDE([Revenue YoY Change], [Revenue Previous Year])

DASHBOARD REQUIREMENTS — DAX QUERIES

1. Artist with highest number of streams
EVALUATE
VAR ArtistStats = ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Artist'[ArtistName]), "Total Streams", [Total Streams])
RETURN TOPN(1, ArtistStats, [Total Streams], DESC, 'Artist'[ArtistName], ASC)

2. Top 10 artists by total revenue
EVALUATE
VAR ArtistStats = ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Artist'[ArtistName]), "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
RETURN TOPN(10, ArtistStats, [Total Revenue], DESC, 'Artist'[ArtistName], ASC)

3. Revenue by genre
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Artist'[PrimaryGenre], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY [Total Revenue] DESC

4. Album listening activity (streams and minutes)
EVALUATE
VAR AlbumStats = ADDCOLUMNS(SUMMARIZE('Album', 'Album'[AlbumKey], 'Album'[AlbumName]), "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Listening Minutes", CALCULATE(SUM('Music_Streams'[MinutesListened])))
RETURN TOPN(10, AlbumStats, [Total Streams], DESC, 'Album'[AlbumName], ASC)

5. Monthly stream trends
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Date'[Year], 'Date'[MonthNumber], 'Date'[YearMonth], "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY 'Date'[Year] ASC, 'Date'[MonthNumber] ASC

6. Revenue comparison for 2024 and 2025
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Date'[Year], FILTER(ALL('Date'[Year]), 'Date'[Year] IN {2024, 2025}), "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY 'Date'[Year] ASC

7. Revenue and average revenue by subscription type
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[SubscriptionType], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue], "Average Revenue per Record", [Average Revenue per Record], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records])
ORDER BY [Total Revenue] DESC

8. Streaming activity by device
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[Device], "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records], "Listening Minutes", CALCULATE(SUM('Music_Streams'[MinutesListened])))
ORDER BY [Total Streams] DESC

9. Listening behaviour by country
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[ListenerCountry], "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Unique Listeners", [Unique Listeners], "Listening Minutes", CALCULATE(SUM('Music_Streams'[MinutesListened])), "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY [Total Streams] DESC

10. Streams by playlist source
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[PlaylistSource], "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records])
ORDER BY [Total Streams] DESC

11. Completed versus not-completed records
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[IsCompleted], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records], "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY 'Music_Streams'[IsCompleted] ASC

12. Skip behaviour by rating
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[Rating], "Average Skip Count", AVERAGE('Music_Streams'[SkipCount]), "Total Skips", [Total Skips], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records])
ORDER BY 'Music_Streams'[Rating] ASC

13. Yearly revenue and year-over-year growth
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Date'[Year], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue], "Previous Year Revenue", [Revenue Previous Year], "YoY Revenue Change", [Revenue YoY Change], "YoY Revenue Growth %", [Revenue YoY Growth %])
ORDER BY 'Date'[Year] ASC

14. High-stream, low-revenue-per-stream artists (top quartile of streams, below overall revenue-per-stream benchmark)
EVALUATE
VAR ArtistStats = ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Artist'[ArtistName]), "Total Streams", [Total Streams], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue], "Revenue per Stream", [Revenue per Stream])
VAR StreamThreshold = PERCENTILEX.INC(ArtistStats, [Total Streams], 0.75)
VAR OverallRevenuePerStream = [Revenue per Stream]
RETURN FILTER(ArtistStats, [Total Streams] >= StreamThreshold && [Revenue per Stream] < OverallRevenuePerStream)
ORDER BY [Total Streams] DESC

DAX QUERY REQUIREMENTS — 15 QUERIES

1. Ten artists with fewest social media followers
EVALUATE
TOPN(10, SELECTCOLUMNS('Artist', "Artist", 'Artist'[ArtistName], "Social Followers", 'Artist'[SocialFollowers]), [Social Followers], ASC, [Artist], ASC)

2. Five oldest albums by release date
EVALUATE
TOPN(5, SELECTCOLUMNS('Album', "Album", 'Album'[AlbumName], "Album Key", 'Album'[AlbumKey], "Release Date", 'Album'[ReleaseDate]), [Release Date], ASC, [Album Key], ASC)

3. Streaming record count, average listening minutes, maximum and minimum rating in one row
EVALUATE
ROW("Total Streaming Records", [Streaming Records], "Average Listening Minutes", [Average Listening Minutes], "Maximum Rating", CALCULATE(MAX('Music_Streams'[Rating])), "Minimum Rating", CALCULATE(MIN('Music_Streams'[Rating])))

4. Total revenue and average rating by playlist source
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[PlaylistSource], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue], "Average Rating", AVERAGE('Music_Streams'[Rating]))
ORDER BY [Total Revenue] DESC

5. Five tracks with highest total StreamCount (artist disambiguates duplicate track names)
EVALUATE
VAR TrackStats = ADDCOLUMNS(SUMMARIZE('Music_Streams', 'Artist'[ArtistName], 'Music_Streams'[TrackName]), "Total Streams", [Total Streams])
RETURN TOPN(5, TrackStats, [Total Streams], DESC, 'Music_Streams'[TrackName], ASC)

6. Unique artists per PrimaryGenre
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Artist'[PrimaryGenre], "Unique Artists", DISTINCTCOUNT('Artist'[ArtistKey]))
ORDER BY 'Artist'[PrimaryGenre] ASC

7. Total revenue by ListenerCountry
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[ListenerCountry], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY [Total Revenue] DESC

8. Five countries with the most unique listeners
EVALUATE
VAR CountryStats = ADDCOLUMNS(VALUES('Music_Streams'[ListenerCountry]), "Unique Listeners", [Unique Listeners])
RETURN TOPN(5, CountryStats, [Unique Listeners], DESC, 'Music_Streams'[ListenerCountry], ASC)

9. Average SkipCount by PlaylistSource
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[PlaylistSource], "Average Skip Count", AVERAGE('Music_Streams'[SkipCount]))
ORDER BY [Average Skip Count] DESC

10. Five albums with highest ProductionCostUSD
EVALUATE
TOPN(5, SELECTCOLUMNS('Album', "Album", 'Album'[AlbumName], "Album Key", 'Album'[AlbumKey], "Production Cost USD", 'Album'[ProductionCostUSD]), [Production Cost USD], DESC, [Album Key], ASC)

11. Total revenue per year using Date table
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Date'[Year], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue])
ORDER BY 'Date'[Year] ASC

12. Total skips by Device and PlaylistSource
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[Device], 'Music_Streams'[PlaylistSource], "Total Skips", [Total Skips])
ORDER BY 'Music_Streams'[Device] ASC, 'Music_Streams'[PlaylistSource] ASC

13. Average SocialFollowers by ArtistType
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Artist'[ArtistType], "Average Social Followers", AVERAGE('Artist'[SocialFollowers]))
ORDER BY [Average Social Followers] DESC

14. Country revenue, record count and average revenue per record
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[ListenerCountry], "Total Revenue", [Total Revenue], "Streaming Records", [Streaming Records], "Average Revenue per Record", [Average Revenue per Record])
ORDER BY [Total Revenue] DESC

15. Unique listeners and average listening minutes by SubscriptionType and Device
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS('Music_Streams'[SubscriptionType], 'Music_Streams'[Device], "Unique Listeners", [Unique Listeners], "Average Listening Minutes", [Average Listening Minutes])
ORDER BY 'Music_Streams'[SubscriptionType] ASC, 'Music_Streams'[Device] ASC

NOTES
Average revenue per record is total revenue divided by the number of fact rows in the current filter context. Revenue per stream is revenue divided by summed StreamCount. The high-stream/low-revenue query defines high streams as the top quartile of artists and low revenue as below the overall revenue-per-stream benchmark. The available data contains 1,800 streaming rows from 2024–2025; the Date table covers both calendar years.
